{"error":false,"activeTest":false,"task":{"id":14272383,"type":"Review","status":"Processed","importance":1,"reason":null,"locked":null,"proofId":null,"currentQuestionId":null,"currentQuestionTimestamp":null,"progress":1,"points":4,"passed":1,"rawPointsAwarded":2,"pointsAwarded":2,"mp":null,"mpAwarded":null,"mpDecayRate":null,"student":{"id":57976,"firstName":"Thomas","lastName":"Walker","locale":null,"subscriptionId":"sub_1UO4EsD4gcTFRx9701mbmpsi","sequenceId":16},"course":{"id":145,"name":"Mathematics for Machine Learning"},"topic":{"id":250,"name":"Conditional Statements"},"test":{"id":null,"name":null,"diagnostic":null,"timeLimit":null,"questionCount":null},"created":"2026-10-16T19:10:59.000Z","started":"2026-10-16T21:08:35.000Z","completed":"2026-10-16T21:10:24.000Z","processed":"2026-10-16T21:10:37.000Z","progressStr":"100%","answers":[{"id":62406364,"created":"2026-10-16T21:08:48.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13165,"number":1,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 9:08 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":81884,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12704,"text":"<p>Which of the following statements are true?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  <strong>If</strong> $8 &lt;   10,$ <strong>then</strong> $2 &lt;   3.$ </li><li>  <strong>If</strong> $8 &gt; 10,$ <strong>then</strong> $2 &lt;   3.$ </li><li>  <strong>If</strong> $8 &gt; 10,$ <strong>then</strong> $2 &gt; 3.$ </li></ol>","choice1":"I, II, and III","choice2":"II and III only","choice3":"I only","choice4":"I and II only","choice5":"I and III only","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>An implication $A \\Rightarrow B$ is true <em>unless</em> $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the &quot;promise&quot; is broken.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Statement I is true. The antecedent $8 &lt;   10$ is true, and the consequent $2 &lt;   3$ is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement II is true. The antecedent $8 &gt; 10$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is <em>not</em> broken, and the statement is true.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent $8 &gt; 10$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is <em>not</em> broken, and the statement is true.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is &quot;I, II, and III.&quot;</p>\n","topic":{"id":250,"name":"Conditional Statements"},"example":{"id":12704,"title":"Identifying True Conditional Statements"},"group":{"id":24109,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272383,"answer":{"id":62406364,"cread":"2026-10-16T21:08:48.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13165},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62406371,"created":"2026-10-16T21:09:02.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11575,"number":2,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 9:09 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":82070,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12704,"text":"<p>Which of the following statements are true?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  <strong>If</strong> $5$ is a prime number, <strong>then</strong> $ 4$ is a composite number. </li><li>  <strong>If</strong> $4$ is a prime number, <strong>then</strong> $5$ is a composite number. </li><li>  <strong>If</strong> $5$ is a prime number, <strong>then</strong> $4$ is a prime number. </li></ol>","choice1":"I and II only","choice2":"I only","choice3":"II only","choice4":"None","choice5":"III only","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>An implication $A \\Rightarrow B$ is true <em>unless</em> $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the &quot;promise&quot; is broken.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Statement I is true. The antecedent &quot;$5$ is a prime number&quot; is true, and the consequent &quot;$ 4$ is a composite number&quot; is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement II is true. The antecedent &quot;$4$ is a prime number&quot; is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is <em>not</em> broken, and the statement is true.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement III is false. The antecedent &quot;$5$ is a prime number&quot; is true, and the consequent &quot;$4$ is a prime number&quot; is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is &quot;I and II only.&quot;</p>\n","topic":{"id":250,"name":"Conditional Statements"},"example":{"id":12704,"title":"Identifying True Conditional Statements"},"group":{"id":24477,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14272383,"answer":{"id":62406371,"cread":"2026-10-16T21:09:02.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11575},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62406380,"created":"2026-10-16T21:09:20.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14056,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 9:09 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":103563,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12704,"text":"<p>Which of the following statements are true?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  <strong>If</strong> $3 +4 &lt;   5 ,$ <strong>then</strong> $ 2+7&lt;   5.$ </li><li>  <strong>If</strong> $2+4&lt;   7,$ <strong>then</strong> $1 +5 &lt;   4.$ </li><li>  <strong>If</strong> $2+3&lt;   4,$ <strong>then</strong> $3 +2 &lt;   1.$ </li></ol>","choice1":"I and III only","choice2":"I and II only","choice3":"II and II